import type { ResultBlockData, ResultData } from "../../components/LabFolders/types";

/**
 * The Results page's four blocks, matching EXPERIMENT_BLOCKS one-for-one
 * in id, label and accent so that both pages share the same glass-sphere
 * index and the same block reads the same colour on either page (see
 * labBlockSpheres.ts).
 *
 * Genetic engineering carries real records, transcribed from the team's
 * own write-up and plotted from their own measurements — every figure here
 * is generated by scripts/build-genetic-engineering-figures.py from the
 * spreadsheets in data/genetic-engineering/, and every number quoted below
 * is one that build recomputes and checks against the sheet. The other
 * three blocks are still the original structure-only placeholders.
 *
 * Two things the sources settle that are easy to get wrong when reading
 * the write-up alone, and which the wording below therefore states
 * explicitly rather than inheriting:
 *
 *  - The summer standard curve is read at 830 nm (the Rousser
 *    molybdenum-blue method). The 600 nm quoted in the write-up belongs to
 *    the later malachite-green assay — a different measurement.
 *  - The uptake rates of the September assay are fitted over the last 45
 *    minutes of the time course, not over all of it. Over the full window
 *    the wild type fits steeper than the transformant, so the window is
 *    what gives the result its direction and is named everywhere it is
 *    quoted. This is flagged for the team to confirm; see the Discussion
 *    of the transformant record.
 */

